        "original_id": "34f772bd-2588-52c0-8e19-444fbba3ed52",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Russia, United Kingdom\n- Events: World War I, World War II, Cold War, Russian Revolution, February Revolution\n- People: Nicholas II\n- Governments: Russian Empire, Provisional Government\n\nFacts:\n- In February 1917 according to the Julian calendar, or March 1917 according to the Gregorian calendar, the February Revolution caused the Russian Empire to collapse.\n- In 1917, Emperor Nicholas II abdicated during the Russian Revolution.\n- In 1917, the old regime in Russia was replaced by a Provisional Government during the first revolution of that year.\n- Russia and the United Kingdom were allies in World War I, but their relations were strained by the Russian Revolution of 1917.\n- Russia and the United Kingdom were allies again in World War II.\n- Russia and the United Kingdom were adversaries during the Cold War from 1947 to 1991.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "2a5ec832-7f08-570a-aed0-b9085bc31563",
        "text": "Page: Russia–United Kingdom relations. Sentence: They were allies again in World Wars I and II, although relations were strained by the Russian Revolution of 1917.\nPage: Russia–United Kingdom relations. Sentence: They were at sword's point during the Cold War (1947–91).\nPage: Russian Revolution. Sentence: The Russian Empire collapsed with the abdication of Emperor Nicholas II and the old regime was replaced by a provisional government during the first revolution of February 1917 (March in the Gregorian calendar; the older Julian calendar was in use in Russia at the time).",
